From 5576e1eeff02158fe655fd9c918755eef8315ca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gary Lin <glin@suse.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:56:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] mfa: wipe key buffer on file read error
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In file_recover_key(), if grub_file_read() fails or returns a short read,
read_buffer is freed without zeroing it first. If a partial key was read
before an error occurred, sensitive key material could remain in freed heap
memory.

Zero the buffer with grub_memset() before calling grub_free(), matching
the behavior of password_recover_key() and mfa_recover_key().

Fixes: 40a1f9e5b627 ("key_protector: Add MFA key protector")
Assisted-by: Gemini:gemini-3.8-flash
Signed-off-by: Gary Lin <glin@suse.com>
Reviewed-by: Avnish Chouhan <avnish@linux.ibm.com>

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gnu-grub/grub/-/merge_requests/306>
---
 grub-core/commands/mfa.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/grub-core/commands/mfa.c b/grub-core/commands/mfa.c
index 53e706ac8..c8cdafaa9 100644
--- a/grub-core/commands/mfa.c
+++ b/grub-core/commands/mfa.c
@@ -316,6 +316,7 @@ file_recover_key (grub_uint8_t **key, grub_size_t *key_size)
   read_n = grub_file_read (file, read_buffer, *key_size);
   if (read_n != *key_size)
     {
+      grub_memset (read_buffer, 0, *key_size);
       grub_free (read_buffer);
       err = grub_error (GRUB_ERR_FILE_READ_ERROR, N_("could not retrieve file contents: %s"), filepath);
       goto error;
